{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And this is the matter of the release.</b> When the blessed El said, ״והשביעת תשמטנה״ (Exodus 23:11), the intent was that a release of loans be made, as it says: ״שמוט כל בעל משה ידו״." "<b>That he proclaimed a release.</b> The blessed El, in saying ״תשמטנה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "Sforno reads the Exodus command to rest the land on the seventh year as also intending a release of debts, linking it to the phrase שמוט כל בעל משה ידו (from Deuteronomy 15:3)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:28.625088132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}